  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#InvestmentGoal">
    <rdfs:label>Investment Goal</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Unified investment goal entity consolidating goal definition, progress tracking, performance metrics, and risk metrics. Provides a complete view of investor goals including target amounts, current progress, returns, and volatility. Replaces separate GoalTracking, GoalPerformance, and GoalRiskMetrics entities.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_ENTITY_INVESTMENT_GOAL_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>investment_goal</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Investment Goal</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Entity</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_ENTITY_INVESTMENT_GOAL_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides unified view of investor financial goals including definition, progress tracking, performance metrics, and risk metrics. Enables goal-based advisory, progress monitoring, and goal achievement forecasting.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>goal_progress_tracking</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>goal_performance_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>goal_risk_assessment</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>financial_planning</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>goal_achievement_forecasting</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "is_on_track", "display_name": "Is On Track", "description": "Whether goal progress is on track (progress &gt;= expected based on time)", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "risk_return_ratio", "display_name": "Risk-Return Ratio", "description": "Return divided by volatility", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#PortfolioHolding">
    <rdfs:label>Portfolio Holding</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Individual investment positions held by investors. Contains cost basis, current valuations, returns, and classification by sector/segment/category. Primary fact table for portfolio analytics and performance tracking.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HOLDING_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>portfolio_holding</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Portfolio Holding</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Entity</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HOLDING_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Core transactional data for portfolio composition analysis, performance  tracking, and asset allocation. Enables queries about what investors own, portfolio value, returns, and diversification.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>portfolio_composition</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>performance_tracking</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>return_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>sector_exposure</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>asset_allocation</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "absolute_return", "display_name": "Absolute Return", "description": "Absolute profit/loss amount", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "holding_period_days", "display_name": "Holding Period (Days)", "description": "Number of days since purchase", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "is_profitable", "display_name": "Is Profitable", "description": "Whether holding is in profit", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#SectorAllocation">
    <rdfs:label>Sector Allocation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Pre-computed sector allocation percentages and total investments per sector for each investor. This is stored data (not computed at runtime) providing fast access to allocation analysis without recalculating from holdings.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_ENTITY_SECTOR_ALLOCATION_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>sector_allocation</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Sector Allocation</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Entity</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_ENTITY_SECTOR_ALLOCATION_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides pre-computed sector allocation breakdown for portfolio analysis and compliance checking. Enables fast queries for allocation percentages, concentration analysis, and diversification assessment.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>allocation_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>concentration_risk</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>diversification_check</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>compliance_validation</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>rebalancing_input</schema1:useCase>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#TimeHorizonContext">
    <rdfs:label>Time Horizon Rules</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Investment time horizon classification with embedded business intelligence including asset allocation strategies, product eligibility rules, liquidity requirements, and risk-return optimization guidelines. Enables duration-based portfolio construction and maturity planning.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_CONTEXT_TIME_HORIZON_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>time_horizon_context</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Time Horizon Rules</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Context</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_CONTEXT_TIME_HORIZON_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides prescriptive business intelligence for duration-based investing. Enables time-appropriate asset allocation, product selection, and exit strategy planning based on investment horizon.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>duration_based_allocation</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>product_eligibility_check</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>liquidity_planning</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>exit_strategy_planning</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>lock_in_compliance</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Very Short Term :: Investments needed within 12 months</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Short Term :: Investments with 1-3 year horizon</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Medium Term :: Investments with 3-7 year horizon</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Long Term :: Investments with 7-15 year horizon</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Very Long Term :: Investments with 15+ year horizon</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>allows_equity :: Whether time horizon allows equity investments</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>max_equity_allowed :: Maximum equity allocation for this horizon</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>requires_liquidity :: Whether liquidity is a key requirement</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>can_use_lock_in_products :: Whether lock-in products like ELSS/PPF are suitable</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_wealth_creation_suitable :: Whether horizon is suitable for wealth creation</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#SegmentContext">
    <rdfs:label>Segment Context</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Business intelligence for market capitalization segments including risk characteristics, allocation guidelines, liquidity profiles, and suitability rules. Enables segment-based compliance and recommendation.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_CONTEXT_SEGMENT_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>segment_context</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Segment Context</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Context</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_CONTEXT_SEGMENT_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides business intelligence for market cap segment-based portfolio analysis including risk characteristics, allocation guidelines, and suitability rules. Enables compliance checking for segment-based allocation limits.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>segment_allocation_compliance</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>risk_assessment</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>liquidity_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>portfolio_construction</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Large Cap :: Companies with market cap above ₹20,000 crores</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Mid Cap :: Companies with market cap between ₹5,000-20,000 crores</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Small Cap :: Companies with market cap below ₹5,000 crores</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Multi Cap :: Funds investing across market cap segments</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_suitable_for_risk_tolerance :: Whether segment is suitable for given risk tolerance</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>allocation_limit_for_risk :: Maximum allocation for given risk tolerance</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#RebalancingAction">
    <rdfs:label>Rebalancing Action</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Time-stamped portfolio rebalancing action events. Captures buy/sell/hold recommendations generated by rebalancing logic. Each event represents an actionable step to align portfolio with target allocation.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_EVENT_REBALANCING_ACTION_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>rebalancing_action</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Rebalancing Action</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Event</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_EVENT_REBALANCING_ACTION_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Captures portfolio rebalancing recommendations and actions. Enables tracking of buy/sell/hold decisions, allocation drift analysis, and rebalancing strategy execution.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>rebalancing_tracking</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>allocation_drift_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>action_recommendations</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>portfolio_adjustment</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>compliance_audit</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "allocation_drift", "display_name": "Allocation Drift", "description": "Difference between current and target allocation", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "drift_direction", "display_name": "Drift Direction", "description": "Whether allocation is overweight or underweight", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#RiskToleranceContext">
    <rdfs:label>Risk Tolerance Rules</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Risk tolerance classification with embedded business intelligence including asset allocation limits, product suitability rules, volatility thresholds, and compliance requirements. This is NOT just a lookup table - it contains the rules that govern how each risk profile should be treated in portfolio construction and compliance validation.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_CONTEXT_RISK_TOLERANCE_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>risk_tolerance_context</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Risk Tolerance Rules</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Context</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_CONTEXT_RISK_TOLERANCE_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides prescriptive business intelligence for risk-based portfolio management. Enables automated compliance checking, suitability validation, and risk-appropriate product recommendations.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>portfolio_compliance</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>suitability_assessment</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>asset_allocation_validation</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>product_recommendation</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>risk_based_rebalancing</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Conservative :: Capital preservation focused with minimal volatility tolerance</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Moderate :: Balanced approach between growth and capital preservation</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Aggressive :: Growth focused with high volatility tolerance</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_equity_heavy_allowed :: Whether equity-heavy portfolios are permitted</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>max_equity_allocation :: Maximum allowed equity allocation percentage</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_high_risk_products_allowed :: Whether high-risk products can be recommended</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>get_suitable_products :: Returns list of suitable product types</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#InvestmentGoalContext">
    <rdfs:label>Investment Goal Rules</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Investment goal classification with embedded business intelligence including recommended asset allocations, target return expectations, time horizon requirements, milestone tracking rules, and priority-based contribution strategies. Enables goal-based portfolio construction and progress monitoring.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_CONTEXT_INVESTMENT_GOAL_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>investment_goal_context</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Investment Goal Rules</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Context</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_CONTEXT_INVESTMENT_GOAL_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides prescriptive business intelligence for goal-based investing. Enables automated goal tracking, asset allocation recommendations based on goal type, and progress milestone monitoring.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>goal_based_portfolio_construction</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>progress_tracking</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>contribution_planning</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>goal_priority_management</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>milestone_alerts</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Retirement :: Long-term wealth accumulation for post-retirement income</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Education :: Goal-dated investment for child's education expenses</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Wealth Creation :: Long-term wealth building without specific end date</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Emergency Fund :: Highly liquid reserve for unexpected expenses</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Home Purchase :: Goal-dated saving for property down payment</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Tax Saving :: Investments primarily for tax benefit under Section 80C</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_long_term_goal :: Whether goal requires long-term investment horizon</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>recommended_equity_allocation :: Recommended equity allocation for the goal</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_tax_advantaged :: Whether goal investments qualify for tax benefits</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>requires_liquidity :: Whether goal requires highly liquid investments</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#SectorContext">
    <rdfs:label>Sector Context</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Business intelligence for industry sectors including risk characteristics, allocation limits by risk tolerance, volatility profiles, and regulatory considerations. This is NOT just a lookup table - it contains embedded business rules that travel with data.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_CONTEXT_SECTOR_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>sector_context</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Sector Context</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Context</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_CONTEXT_SECTOR_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides business intelligence for sector-based portfolio analysis including risk characteristics, allocation limits, and suitability rules. Enables automated compliance checking and intelligent recommendations.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>allocation_compliance</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>risk_assessment</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>suitability_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>rebalancing_rules</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>portfolio_enrichment</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Technology :: Information technology, software, hardware, and tech services</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Financial Services :: Banks, insurance, asset management, fintech</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Healthcare :: Pharmaceuticals, medical devices, healthcare services</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Consumer Goods :: FMCG, consumer durables, retail</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Energy :: Oil &amp; gas, renewable energy, power generation</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Utilities :: Electric, gas, water utilities</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Real Estate :: REITs, property development, real estate services</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_suitable_for_conservative :: Whether sector is suitable for conservative investors</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_defensive :: Whether sector is defensive (non-cyclical)</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>max_allocation_for_risk_tolerance :: Maximum allowed allocation for given risk tolerance</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#CashFlow">
    <rdfs:label>Cash Flow</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Time-stamped cash flow events including deposits, withdrawals, SIP contributions, lump sum investments, and redemptions. Primary event source for transaction history, cash flow analysis, and contribution tracking.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_EVENT_CASH_FLOW_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>cash_flow</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Cash Flow</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Event</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_EVENT_CASH_FLOW_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Tracks all monetary transactions for investor portfolios including contributions and withdrawals. Enables cash flow analysis, contribution tracking, and transaction history reporting.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>transaction_history</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>cash_flow_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>contribution_tracking</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>sip_monitoring</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>withdrawal_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "is_inflow", "display_name": "Is Inflow", "description": "Whether this is an inflow (deposit/contribution)", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "absolute_amount", "display_name": "Absolute Amount", "description": "Absolute value of transaction amount", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "transaction_month", "display_name": "Transaction Month", "description": "Month of transaction for grouping", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#ScenarioRebalancing">
    <rdfs:label>Scenario-Based Rebalancing</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Time-stamped scenario-based rebalancing events. Captures rebalancing actions triggered by specific market scenarios (e.g., interest rate changes, market volatility spikes). Each event represents a conditional rebalancing response with rationale and affected assets.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_EVENT_SCENARIO_REBALANCING_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>scenario_rebalancing</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Scenario-Based Rebalancing</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Event</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_EVENT_SCENARIO_REBALANCING_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Captures scenario-driven portfolio rebalancing triggers. Enables tracking of how market events or conditions trigger rebalancing actions, affected assets/sectors, and the rationale behind allocation changes.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>scenario_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>conditional_rebalancing</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>risk_event_tracking</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>market_response_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>compliance_documentation</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "allocation_change", "display_name": "Allocation Change", "description": "Change in allocation from current to new", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "change_direction", "display_name": "Change Direction", "description": "Whether allocation was increased or decreased", "searchable": true}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#InvestmentTypeContext">
    <rdfs:label>Investment Type Rules</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Investment product type classification with embedded business intelligence including tax treatment rules, lock-in requirements, risk-return profiles, expense ratios, and regulatory compliance requirements. Enables product-level compliance checks, tax optimization, and suitability validation.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_CONTEXT_INVESTMENT_TYPE_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>investment_type_context</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Investment Type Rules</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Context</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_CONTEXT_INVESTMENT_TYPE_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides comprehensive business intelligence for investment products. Enables automated tax calculations, lock-in compliance, suitability checks, and regulatory requirement validation.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>tax_planning</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>lock_in_compliance</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>product_recommendation</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>regulatory_compliance</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>expense_optimization</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>redemption_planning</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Equity Mutual Fund :: Open-ended mutual fund investing primarily in equities</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Debt Mutual Fund :: Mutual fund investing in fixed income securities</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>ELSS :: Equity Linked Savings Scheme with 80C tax benefit</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Stock :: Direct equity investment in listed stocks</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>ETF :: Passively managed fund traded on exchange</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>PPF :: Government-backed long-term savings with guaranteed returns</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>NPS :: Government pension scheme with equity and debt options</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>FD :: Bank fixed deposit with guaranteed returns</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>has_lock_in :: Whether investment has mandatory lock-in</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_80c_eligible :: Whether investment qualifies for 80C deduction</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>ltcg_rate :: Long-term capital gains tax rate</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_equity_taxed :: Whether taxed as equity (15% STCG)</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>requires_demat :: Whether demat account is required</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#AssetClassContext">
    <rdfs:label>Asset Class Context</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Unified business intelligence for asset categories and investment types, merging Category (Equity/Debt/Hybrid) and InvestmentType (Mutual Fund/Stock/ ELSS/PPF). Contains risk profiles, tax treatment, lock-in rules, and suitability guidelines.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_CONTEXT_ASSET_CLASS_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>asset_class_context</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Asset Class Context</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Context</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_CONTEXT_ASSET_CLASS_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides comprehensive business intelligence for asset classes combining category characteristics (equity/debt/hybrid) with investment type specifics (mutual fund/stock/ELSS/PPF). Enables tax-aware recommendations, lock-in compliance, and suitability analysis.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>tax_planning</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>lock_in_compliance</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>suitability_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>product_recommendation</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>regulatory_compliance</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Equity Mutual Fund :: Mutual funds investing primarily in equities</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Stock :: Direct equity investment in listed stocks</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>ELSS :: Equity Linked Savings Scheme with tax benefits under 80C</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Debt Mutual Fund :: Mutual funds investing in fixed income securities</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>PPF :: Government-backed long-term savings with guaranteed returns</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>Hybrid Fund :: Funds investing in both equity and debt</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:contextValueEntry>NPS :: Government pension scheme with equity and debt options</schema1:contextValueEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>has_lock_in :: Whether investment has mandatory lock-in period</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_tax_saving :: Whether investment qualifies for 80C deduction</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
    <schema1:derivedContextEntry>is_suitable_for_risk :: Whether asset class suits given risk tolerance</schema1:derivedContextEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#PortfolioHealth">
    <rdfs:label>Portfolio Health</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Pre-computed portfolio health scores across multiple dimensions: goal alignment, risk, liquidity, and diversification. This is stored data (not computed at  runtime) providing instant access to health assessments.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HEALTH_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>portfolio_health</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Portfolio Health</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Entity</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_ENTITY_PORTFOLIO_HEALTH_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides pre-computed health assessment scores for portfolio monitoring, risk management, and advisory prioritization. Enables quick identification of portfolios needing attention.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>portfolio_monitoring</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>health_assessment</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>advisory_prioritization</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>risk_identification</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>client_review</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "overall_health_score", "display_name": "Overall Health Score", "description": "Weighted average of all health dimensions", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
    <schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>{"name": "health_status", "display_name": "Health Status", "description": "Categorical health assessment", "searchable": null}</schema1:derivedAttributeEntry>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/schema-linkage#InvestorProfile">
    <rdfs:label>Investor Profile</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Core investor identity and investment preferences. This is the primary entity for all investor-centric queries including risk profiling, goal setting, and suitability analysis. Contains demographic information, risk tolerance,  investment horizon, and sector preferences.</rdfs:comment>
    <schema1:nodeKind>table</schema1:nodeKind>
    <schema1:sourceId>ATOM_ENTITY_INVESTOR_PROFILE_001</schema1:sourceId>
    <schema1:sourceName>investor_profile</schema1:sourceName>
    <schema1:displayName>Investor Profile</schema1:displayName>
    <schema1:tableSubtype>Entity</schema1:tableSubtype>
    <schema1:yamlFile>TABLE_ENTITY_INVESTOR_PROFILE_001.yaml</schema1:yamlFile>
    <schema1:businessPurpose>Provides the foundational investor identity and preferences required for  portfolio management, suitability analysis, and personalized advisory services. This entity is the anchor for all investor-centric operations.</schema1:businessPurpose>
    <schema1:useCase>investor_lookup</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>suitability_analysis</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>risk_profiling</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>portfolio_construction</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>client_segmentation</schema1:useCase>
    <schema1:useCase>regulatory_reporting</schema1:useCase>
  </owl:Class>
</rdf:RDF>
